{"kind":"stack","id":"s-magnets","title":"Magnets have 2 poles","theme":{"background":"#fff8e7","foreground":"#1f2937","font":"Comic Sans MS, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Magnetic poles"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-e","content":"The two ends of a magnet, where its pull is strongest. Every magnet has a north pole and a south pole."},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-t","content":"Like poles"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-e","content":"When two north poles or two south poles are brought close, they push each other away."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","picto":"magnet"},{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"How many poles does a bar magnet have?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"One","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"Two","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"Three","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"What are the two ends of a magnet called?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"Edges","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"Poles","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-c","label":"Points","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-d","label":"Sides","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-q","content":"Two north poles are brought close together. What happens?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"They stick together","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"They push apart","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-c","label":"Nothing happens","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-q","content":"Your friend has a magnet and a paper clip. Which way should you hold the magnet?"},{"type":"button","id":"c6-a","label":"Hold the north pole near the clip","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"Hold the magnet still, far away","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"The paper clip jumps up to the magnet. Your friend cheers."},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-t","content":"Nothing moves, because the clip is too far from the magnet's pull."},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"Which statement about magnets is true?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"Every magnet has only one pole","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"Every magnet has two poles","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-c","label":"Only big magnets have poles","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-h","content":"Well done, you finished the magnets quiz!"},{"type":"text","id":"c10-m","content":"You now know that magnets have two poles and that like poles push each other away. Keep exploring!"}],"actions":[]}}
